# Camouflage replaces Bot2's declaration of blockers this turn (CR 614.1a, 509.1): Bot2 makes one pile for each of Bot1's two
# attackers, each pile goes to a different attacker at random (the die's face 2 gives the first pile to the second attacker,
# Ornithopter), and each creature in a pile blocks the attacker its pile was given if it can. Phyrexian Walker and Kobolds of
# Kher Keep, given the flying Ornithopter, can't block it (CR 702.9b) and block nothing; Crimson Kobolds, given Memnite,
# blocks it; Crookshank Kobolds, in no pile, blocks nothing, and Bot2 is not also asked to declare blockers. Bot1's creatures are no one's to put in a pile. Camouflage can't
# be cast in Bot1's main phase, nor in Bot2's declare attackers step (CR 601.3: "your declare attackers step"), and on Bot1's
# next turn Bot2 declares blockers as usual: the effect lasted that turn only (CR 611.2a, 514.2).
[Bot1 Deck]
Camouflage
Camouflage
Forest
Forest
Memnite
Ornithopter
Island
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Phyrexian Walker
Kobolds of Kher Keep
Crimson Kobolds
Crookshank Kobolds
Island x14

[Dice]
2

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Phyrexian Walker.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Kobolds of Kher Keep.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Crimson Kobolds.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Crookshank Kobolds.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
! Bot1.Hand.Camouflage.Cast
Bot1.Attack(Memnite > Bot2; Ornithopter > Bot2)
Bot1.Hand.Camouflage.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
! Bot2.Choose(Memnite)
Bot2.Choose(Phyrexian Walker; Kobolds of Kher Keep)
Bot2.Choose(Crimson Kobolds)
! Bot2.Block
? Combat.Blocks = Crimson Kobolds > Memnite
? Combat.Blocks.Count = 1
[T4 Bot2.DeclareAttackers]
Bot2.Attack(Phyrexian Walker > Bot1)
Bot2.Pass
! Bot1.Hand.Camouflage.Cast
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Memnite > Bot2)
Bot2.Block(Crookshank Kobolds > Memnite)
[T5 Bot1.CombatDamage]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 20
Bot2.Graveyard = Crookshank Kobolds; Crimson Kobolds
